1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,320
WOMAN: I've been meaning to ask you for some advice about restaurants.

2
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:08,216
WOMAN: I need to book somewhere to celebrate my sister's 30th birthday

3
00:00:08,216 --> 00:00:13,010
and I liked the sound of that place you went to for your mum's 50th.

4
00:00:13,010 --> 00:00:17,617
MAN: The Junction? Yeah, I'd definitely recommend that for a special occasion.

5
00:00:17,617 --> 00:00:21,160
We had a great time there. Everyone really enjoyed it.

6
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:24,270
WOMAN: Where is it again? I can't remember.

7
00:00:24,270 --> 00:00:29,050
MAN: It's on Greyson Street, only about a two minute walk from the station.

8
00:00:29,050 --> 00:00:30,500
WOMAN: Oh, that's good.

9
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:32,900
I'd prefer not to have to drive anywhere

10
00:00:33,440 --> 00:00:36,590
But I don't want to have to walk too far either.

11
00:00:36,590 --> 00:00:42,490
MAN: Yes, the location's perfect but that's not necessarily why I'd recommend it.

12
00:00:42,490 --> 00:00:50,570
MAN: The food's amazing. If you like fish it's probably the best restaurant in town for that.

13
00:00:50,570 --> 00:00:56,128
MAN: It's always really fresh and there are lots of interesting dishes to choose from.

14
00:00:56,128 --> 00:00:58,560
But all the food is good there.

15
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:01,060
WOMAN: Is it really expensive?

16
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:06,640
MAN: It's certainly not cheap but for a special occasion I think it's fine.

17
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:08,380
MAN: It's got a great atmosphere

18
00:01:08,900 --> 00:01:13,750
and before dinner you can go up on the roof and have a drink.

19
00:01:13,750 --> 00:01:15,340
MAN: It's really nice up there

20
00:01:15,520 --> 00:01:21,280
but you need to book. It's very popular as the views are spectacular.

21
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:25,700
WOMAN: Sounds good. So that's definitely a possibility then

22
00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:28,960
Is there anywhere else you can think of?

23
00:01:28,960 --> 00:01:34,790
MAN: If you want somewhere a bit less formal then you could try Paloma.

24
00:01:34,790 --> 00:01:36,930
WOMAN: Where's that? I haven't heard of it.

25
00:01:36,930 --> 00:01:38,894
MAN: No, it's quite new.

26
00:01:38,894 --> 00:01:44,130
It's only been open a few months but it's got a great reputation already.

27
00:01:44,130 --> 00:01:47,730
It's in a really beautiful old building on Bow Street.

28
00:01:47,730 --> 00:01:52,760
WOMAN: Oh, I think I know where you mean - right beside the cinema?

29
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:56,580
MAN: Yes, that's it. I've only been there a couple of times

30
00:01:56,580 --> 00:01:59,060
but I was really impressed.

31
00:01:59,060 --> 00:02:02,360
MAN: The chef used to work at Don Felipe's, apparently

32
00:02:02,940 --> 00:02:05,640
I was really sorry when that closed down.

33
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:08,770
WOMAN: So is all the food they serve Spanish, then?

34
00:02:08,770 --> 00:02:12,260
MAN: Yeah. You can get lots of small dishes to share

35
00:02:12,720 --> 00:02:15,530
which always works really well if you're in a group.

36
00:02:15,530 --> 00:02:17,690
WOMAN: Mmm. Worth thinking about.

37
00:02:17,690 --> 00:02:22,491
MAN: Yeah. There's a lively atmosphere and the waiters are really friendly.

38
00:02:22,491 --> 00:02:28,400
The only thing is that you need to pay a £50 deposit to book a table.

39
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:31,390
WOMAN: A lot of restaurants are doing that these days.

40
00:02:31,390 --> 00:02:37,022
WOMAN: I should have a look at the menu to check there's a good choice of vegetarian dishes.

41
00:02:37,022 --> 00:02:39,690
A couple of my friends have stopped eating meat.

42
00:02:39,690 --> 00:02:44,650
MAN: Not sure. I'd say the selection of those would be quite limited.

43
00:02:44,650 --> 00:02:48,870
MAN: I've just thought of another idea. Have you been to The Audley?

44
00:02:48,870 --> 00:02:53,440
WOMAN: No, don't think I've heard of it. How's it spelt?

45
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:59,860
MAN: A-U-D-L-E-Y. You must have heard of it

46
00:02:59,920 --> 00:03:02,430
there's been a lot about it in the press.

47
00:03:02,430 --> 00:03:05,480
WOMAN: I don't tend to pay much attention to that kind of thing

48
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:08,640
So where is it exactly?

49
00:03:08,640 --> 00:03:13,280
MAN: It's in that hotel near Baxter Bridge - on the top floor.

50
00:03:13,280 --> 00:03:16,710
WOMAN: Oh, the views would be incredible from up there.

51
00:03:16,710 --> 00:03:21,897
MAN: Yeah. I'd love to go. I can't think of the chef's name

52
00:03:21,897 --> 00:03:25,180
but she was a judge on that TV cookery show recently

53
00:03:25,740 --> 00:03:28,380
And she's written a couple of cookery books.

54
00:03:28,380 --> 00:03:30,770
WOMAN: Oh, Angela Frayn.

55
00:03:30,770 --> 00:03:37,010
MAN: That's the one. Anyway, it's had excellent reviews from all the newspapers.

56
00:03:37,010 --> 00:03:40,590
WOMAN: That would be a memorable place for a celebration.

57
00:03:40,590 --> 00:03:45,213
MAN: Definitely. Obviously it's worth going there just for the view

58
00:03:45,213 --> 00:03:48,680
but the food is supposed to be really special.

59
00:03:48,680 --> 00:03:52,770
WOMAN: She only likes cooking with local products, doesn't she?

60
00:03:52,770 --> 00:03:58,897
MAN: Yes. Everything at the restaurant has to be sourced within a short distance

61
00:03:58,897 --> 00:04:01,960
and absolutely nothing flown in from abroad.

62
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:05,050
WOMAN: I imagine it's really expensive though.

63
00:04:05,050 --> 00:04:07,660
MAN: Well, you could go for the set lunch

64
00:04:08,280 --> 00:04:13,548
That's quite reasonable for a top class restaurant: £30 a head.

65
00:04:13,548 --> 00:04:18,000
In the evening I think it'd be more like £50.

66
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:23,198
WOMAN: At least that, I should think. But I'm sure everyone would enjoy it.

67
00:04:23,198 --> 00:04:26,080
It's not the kind of place you leave feeling hungry

68
00:04:26,380 --> 00:04:29,090
though, is it? With tiny portions?

69
00:04:29,090 --> 00:04:35,170
MAN: No, the reviews I've read didn't mention that. I imagine they'd be average.

70
00:04:35,170 --> 00:04:39,010
WOMAN: Well, that's all great, thanks...
